-- statement:
--   The product of all primes $p \le 1049$ — the primorial $1049\#$ — equals
--   $$ exactly, and the product of $p-1$ over the same primes equals
--   $$.
--
--   These exact values extend the primorial certificate at $691$ to the anchor prime $1049$, anchoring the finite verification of the Rosser–Schoenfeld Mertens-product bound (Theorem 23, inequality (4.10)) on the leg $1050 \le x \le 1500$ of the induction towards the five-primes theorem. The values are computed with a sieve of Eratosthenes and exact integer arithmetic.
-- source:
--   Exact integer computation (sieve of Eratosthenes, exact products). Downstream use: J.B. Rosser, L. Schoenfeld, Approximate formulas for some functions of prime numbers, Illinois J. Math. 6 (1962), 64–94, §5, p. 73, Theorem 23 (4.10). Primorial reference: OEIS A002110. https://doi.org/10.1215/ijm/1255631807

